  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/validate.cc",
    "description": "In ValidateArrayDataVisitor::Visit(const UnionArray&), dense-union validation dereferences offsets[i] without first verifying that the union has a valid offsets buffer for the declared array length. For malformed IPC input, a UnionArray can be constructed with inconsistent/missing/truncated offset data, so reading raw_value_offsets()[i] causes an out-of-bounds heap read (ASan crash at validate.cc:380).",
    "conditions": "The arrow-ipc-stream-fuzz harness calls ipc::internal::FuzzIpcStream(), which opens attacker-controlled IPC stream bytes and reads RecordBatches, then calls RecordBatch::ValidateFull() -> internal::ValidateArrayData() -> ValidateArrayDataVisitor::Visit(UnionArray). The PoV must produce a dense UnionArray with non-null elements and an invalid/undersized offsets buffer relative to array.length(), so the loop over i reads offsets[i] past the buffer."
  },
